-- title:
--   Central, odd and even elements of the away-unit group
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\mathbb H_2 := \mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_2,b_2]$ denotes the definite quaternion algebra occurring below, $F_1 := \,$[`ValuationSubring.ratClosure A₁`](def/ValuationSubring_CompletionRatClosure.html#L13) the closure of the prime field inside the completion of $A_1$ at its valuation, $\iota_1^{\times}$ the map on unit groups induced by the embedding $\iota_1 \colon \mathbb H_2 \to M_2(F_1)$, and
--   $$\tilde\Gamma := \mathtt{CosetGraph.awayUnits}\ R_2\ v_1 = \bigcap_{w \neq v_1}\ \{x \in \mathbb H_2^{\times} : \text{the image of } x \text{ in } (\mathbb H_2 \otimes_{\mathbb Q} \mathbb Q_w)^{\times} \text{ lies in the subgroup generated by } \mathtt{localBoxUnits}\ R_2\ w\},$$
--   the group of units of $\mathbb H_2$ that are locally integral, with integral inverse, at every height-one prime other than $v_1$.
--
--   Numerical data: a nonzero squarefree $N$ (`hN`), primes $q,q'$ with $q'\neq q$ (`hqq'`), neither dividing $N$ (`hqN`, `hq'N`), both at least $5$ (`hq5`, `hq'5`), and a nonzero $D$ with $2Nqq' \mid D$ (`hD`). Further, a valuation subring $A_1$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q'$ in the sense that $q'$ is a nonunit of $A_1$ (`hA₁`), whose decomposition subgroup over $\mathbb Q$ acts by valuation-preserving automorphisms (`hiso₁`), and a height-one prime $v_1$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ containing $q'$ (`hv₁`).
--
--   Definite side: rationals $a_2,b_2$ with $a_2<0$, $b_2<0$ and such that $\mathbb H_2 \otimes_{\mathbb Q} \mathbb Q_v$ is a division algebra exactly for the $v$ containing $q$ (`hdef₂`); a maximal order $\Lambda_2$ (`hΛ₂`), an order $R_2 \le \Lambda_2$ (`hRΛ₂`) which is an intersection of two maximal orders of relative index $N$ (`hR₂`); a finite idele $n_2 \in \mathtt{primeHeckeSet}\ R_2\ q'$ (`hn₂`) such that $\mathtt{meetOrder}\ R_2\ n_2 = R_2 \cap n_2R_2n_2^{-1}$ is again an intersection of two maximal orders, of relative index $Nq'$ (`hS₂`), is stable under conjugation by $n_2$ (`hnorm₂`), and such that the shift by $n_2$ on the class set of the finite-idele stabiliser of $\mathtt{meetOrder}\ R_2\ n_2$ is an involution (`hsq₂`); finiteness of the two class sets involved; and `hlaws₂`, the conjunction of the four Hecke compatibilities of `ClassSetHeckeLaws` (commutation of the edge operators, commutation of the vertex operators, intertwining of edge and vertex operators away from $q'$ through the two degeneracy pushforwards, and preservation of the joint kernel).
--
--   Indefinite side: rationals $a,b$ with $0<a$ or $0<b$ and such that $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ is locally a division algebra exactly at the primes containing $q$ or $q'$ (`hB`), together with a maximal order $\Lambda$ (`hΛ`).
--
--   Moduli data over $\mathbb Z[1/D] = \mathtt{Localization.Away}\ D$: a field $\bar F$, a curve over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in the sense of `IsCurveOver` (principal divisors of degree zero, finite residue extensions, free rank-one module of Kähler differentials) and essentially of finite type; a scheme $X$ with a morphism $\pi_X$ to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb Z[1/D]$; a $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-point $\bar s$ of the base; an assignment `pt` sending a fake elliptic curve over $S$ with $\Lambda$-action and level-$N$ structure to an $S$-point of $X$ over the base, subject to the coarse-moduli clauses `pt_iso`, `pt_pullback`, `pt_surjective`, `pt_injective` (invariance under isomorphism, compatibility with base change, and bijectivity on isomorphism classes over algebraically closed fields); a curve model $\mathfrak M$ of $\bar F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with an isomorphism $e_{\mathfrak M}$ onto the fibre product of $\pi_X$ and $\bar s$ compatible with the structure morphisms (`he𝔐`); semilinear Galois actions `gal` on $\bar F$; tower data $\mathbb T$ for the primes away from $q,q'$ with Galois actions `galT`; pairs of semilinear automorphisms $W$, $WT$; and a witness `tw` of `ModuliTowerWitnessD`, whose fields (summarised here) provide representative fake elliptic curves for the places of $\bar F$ and of the tower fields, their compatibility with `pt`, $\mathfrak M$ and the degeneracy maps of the tower, and the normalisations of `gal`, `galT`, $W$, $WT$ on the base field.
--
--   Local data at $q'$: an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra map $\iota_1 \colon \mathbb H_2 \to M_2(F_1)$ (`hι₁`), the induced projective representation $\rho_1$ into $\mathrm{PGL}_2(F_1)$ given by projectivising $\iota_1^{\times}$ (`hρ₁`); a pseudo-uniformizer $\varpi_1$ of $F_1$ in the completion whose image is $q'$ (`hϖ₁`), with the holomorphic ring attached to $\varpi_1$ and $\rho_1$ a domain; an isometric action `dIso₁` of the decomposition subgroup on the completion realising the Galois action (`hdIso₁`); a character $\chi$ of the decomposition subgroup with values in $\mathbb Z/2$ that is trivial on inertia (`hχ₁`), nontrivial on every Frobenius at $q'$ (`hχ₂`), and whose kernel consists exactly of the elements fixing all $x$ in the residue field of $A_1$ with $x^{q'^2}=x$ (`hχ₃`).
--
--   Coefficient rings: a characteristic-zero discrete valuation ring $\mathcal O_0$ with irreducible $\pi$ (`hπ`), $(\pi)$-adically complete (`hcpl`), residue field of cardinality $q'$ (`hres`), with $(q') = (\pi)$ (`hunr`), and with $F_1$ as fraction field; an $\mathcal O_0$-algebra $Onr$ with an $\mathcal O_0$-automorphism $Fr$, which is $\pi$-adically complete (`hOc`), has $(\pi)$ maximal (`hOm`), is integral modulo $\pi$ (`hOa`), has a root modulo $\pi$ for every monic polynomial of positive degree (`hOcl`), and satisfies $Fr(x)\equiv x^{q'} \pmod{\pi}$ (`hFr`); a homomorphism $vdet \colon \mathrm{GL}_2(F_1) \to \mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) characterised by $vdet(g) = \mathrm{ofAdd}(n)$ if and only if $\det g = u\pi^{n}$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal O_0$ (`hvdet`); a ring map $\psi_0 \colon Onr \to$ the completion with values in the valuation ring (`hψ₀`) and compatible with $\mathcal O_0$ (`hψ₀𝒪`); and the normalisations $\pi \mapsto \varpi_1$ (`hπϖ`), $N$ a unit of $\mathcal O_0$ (`hN₀`), identification of the image of $\mathcal O_0$ with the valuation ring of $F_1$ (`h𝒪₀`), and the rank-one property `hrk` of the valuation.
--
--   Integral models and uniformisation: a scheme $\mathcal X_0$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O_0$ with point assignment $pt_0$ which is a coarse moduli space for fake elliptic curves with $\Lambda$-action and level-$N$ structure (`h𝒳₀`), with $\mathcal X_0$ integral and $f_0$ flat, separated, locally of finite type and quasi-compact; for each prime $\ell$ away from $q'$ and $q$ a scheme $\mathcal Y_0(\ell)$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O_0$ which is a coarse moduli space for such objects with extra level $\ell$ (`h𝒴₀`); degeneracy morphisms $d_{00},d_{10}$ over the base (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`) inducing on moduli the forgetting of the extra level (`hd₀`) and the quotient by a level-$\ell$ isogeny (`hd₁`); endomorphisms $ar$, $arbar$ of $\mathcal X_0$ over the base (`harf`, `harbarf`) inducing the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $q'$ and at $q$ respectively (`har`, `harbar`); and maps $\Theta$, $\Theta T$ from the functor of pairs $(\psi,d)$, with $\psi \colon Onr \to B$ an $\mathcal O_0$-algebra map and $d$ a Deligne datum over $B$, to the $B$-points of $f_0$, resp. of $g_0(\ell)$, defined for $\mathcal O_0$-algebras $B$ in which $\pi$ is nilpotent. The hypothesis `hCD` (twelve clauses, summarised here) states: naturality of $\Theta$ and of each $\Theta T(\ell)$; invariance of $\Theta$ under the twisted action of elements of $\tilde\Gamma$ and of $\Theta T(\ell)$ under that of $\tilde\Gamma \cap s_1(\ell)\tilde\Gamma s_1(\ell)^{-1}$; over an algebraically closed field with $\pi$ nilpotent, surjectivity of $\Theta$ and of $\Theta T(\ell)$ in the second variable together with the identification of their fibres with the twisted orbits of these groups; the initiality of $\Theta$, resp. $\Theta T(\ell)$, among invariant natural transformations into the nilpotent points of an arbitrary base morphism; the compatibility of $\Theta T(\ell)$ with $d_{00}$ and, through the twisted action of $s_1(\ell)$, with $d_{10}$; and the compatibility of $\Theta$ with $ar$ via the Frobenius twist by $1$ in the first coordinate and with $arbar$ via the twisted action of $\bar w_1(\text{none})$.
--
--   Arithmetic-group data: families $s_1(\ell) \in \mathbb H_2^{\times}$ and $sf_1(\ell)$ in the finite-idele units, indexed by the primes $\ell \notin \{q,q'\}$, such that (`hs₁`) at every height-one prime $u$ not containing $q'$ the $u$-component of $sf_1(\ell)$ is $s_1(\ell)\otimes 1$, at every $u$ containing $q'$ it is $1$, the product of the diagonal idele of the central rational $\ell$ with $sf_1(\ell)^{-1}$ lies in $\mathtt{levelHeckeUSet}\ \Lambda_2\ (\mathtt{meetOrder}\ R_2\ n_2)\ \ell$ when $\ell \mid N$ and in $\mathtt{primeHeckeSet}\ (\mathtt{meetOrder}\ R_2\ n_2)\ \ell$ otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_1(\ell)) = \ell$; a family of subgroups $\Gamma_1$ indexed by $\mathrm{Option}$ of these primes with $\Gamma_1(\text{none}) = \{x \in \tilde\Gamma : \mathrm{ord}_{q'}(\mathrm{nrd}\,x) \text{ even}\}$ (`hΓ₁0`) and $\Gamma_1(\text{some }\ell) = \Gamma_1(\text{none}) \cap s_1(\ell)\Gamma_1(\text{none})s_1(\ell)^{-1}$ (`hΓ₁ℓ`); elements $w_1$ with $w_1(\text{none}) \in \tilde\Gamma$ of reduced norm $q'$ and $w_1(\text{some }\ell)$ in the corresponding away-unit group of $\mathtt{meetOrder}\ R_2\ (sf_1 \ell)$ of reduced norm $q'$ (`hw₁`); and elements $\bar w_1$ with $\mathrm{nrd}\,\bar w_1 = q$, locally a unit of the relevant local box at every height-one prime $u \neq v_1$ not containing $q$, and normalising both the local box of $R_2$ (resp. of $\mathtt{meetOrder}\ R_2\ (sf_1 \ell)$) and that of $\Lambda_2$ at every $u \neq v_1$ (`hwbar₁`).
--
--   Under these hypotheses the following six assertions hold.
--
--   (i) There exist $z \in \tilde\Gamma$ and $c \in F_1$ such that $\iota_1^{\times}(z)$, viewed as a matrix, equals $c\cdot 1$, and $vdet(\iota_1^{\times}(z)) = \mathrm{ofAdd}(2)$.
--
--   (ii) There exists $w \in \tilde\Gamma$ with $vdet(\iota_1^{\times}(w)) = \mathrm{ofAdd}(1)$.
--
--   (iii) For every $x \in \mathbb H_2^{\times}$: $x \in \Gamma_1(\text{none})$ if and only if $x \in \tilde\Gamma$ and $\mathrm{toAdd}\,vdet(\iota_1^{\times}(x))$ is even.
--
--   (iv) For every prime $\ell$ distinct from $q'$ and $q$ there exist $z$ in $\tilde\Gamma \cap s_1(\ell)\tilde\Gamma s_1(\ell)^{-1}$ and $c \in F_1$ with $\iota_1^{\times}(z) = c\cdot 1$ as a matrix and $vdet(\iota_1^{\times}(z)) = \mathrm{ofAdd}(2)$.
--
--   (v) For every such $\ell$ there exists $w \in \tilde\Gamma \cap s_1(\ell)\tilde\Gamma s_1(\ell)^{-1}$ with $vdet(\iota_1^{\times}(w)) = \mathrm{ofAdd}(1)$.
--
--   (vi) For every such $\ell$ and every $x \in \mathbb H_2^{\times}$: $x \in \Gamma_1(\text{some }\ell)$ if and only if $x \in \tilde\Gamma \cap s_1(\ell)\tilde\Gamma s_1(\ell)^{-1}$ and $\mathrm{toAdd}\,vdet(\iota_1^{\times}(x))$ is even.
--
--   In (iv)–(vi) the prime $\ell$ runs over `HeckeTower.AwayPrime q' q`, and $s_1$ and $\Gamma_1$ are evaluated at the same prime reindexed as an element of `HeckeTower.AwayPrime q q'`.
--
--   This is a bookkeeping step on the $q'$-adic side of the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation of the Shimura curve of level $N$ attached to the indefinite algebra ramified exactly at $q$ and $q'$: it re-expresses the arithmetic groups $\Gamma_1$, defined by the parity of the $q'$-adic valuation of the reduced norm, through the determinant valuation `vdet` on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the local field $F_1$, and records a central element of `vdet`-value $2$ and an element of `vdet`-value $1$ in the away-unit group, both at the base level and at every extra-level prime. It is used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.exists_mumfordEmbedding_of_cerednikDrinfeld_uniformization_one_zero_of_two_mul_dvd`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.exists_mumfordEmbedding_of_cerednikDrinfeld_uniformization_one_zero_of_two_mul_dvd), where these data feed the Mumford-curve description of the special fibre.
